      "title": "Cartoonist sues AI meme generator monetizing his work",
      "content_html": "<a href=\"https://boingboing.net/2026/07/29/cartoonist-sues-ai-meme-generator-monetizing-his-work.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Cartoonist sues AI meme generator monetizing his work\"><img alt=\"Images: Superelmer on Facebook\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"544\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/boingboing.net/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Images-Superelmer.jpg?fit=1080%2C544&amp;quality=60&amp;ssl=1\" style=\"display: block; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 5px;\" width=\"1080\" /></a><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1117821\" height=\"581\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/boingboing.net/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/usc-1.jpg?resize=930%2C581&#038;quality=60&#038;ssl=1\" width=\"930\" /></figure>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Replacing the text in popular comic strips is <a href=\"https://boingboing.net/2007/06/29/all-memes-one-comic.html\">a common meme format</a>, and few artists are displeased to see their work mutating online. Websites can <a href=\"https://imgflip.com/memegenerator/Running-Away-Balloon\">generate these pics</a> for users lacking image-editing skills. But when sites seek payment, <a href=\"https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2020/02/success-kids-mom-wont-stand-for-steve-kings-meme-ad/\">a line is crossed</a>. &#8212; <a class=\"read-more\" href=\"https://boingboing.net/2026/07/29/cartoonist-sues-ai-meme-generator-monetizing-his-work.html\">Read the rest </a></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://boingboing.net/2026/07/29/cartoonist-sues-ai-meme-generator-monetizing-his-work.html\">Cartoonist sues AI meme generator monetizing his work</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://boingboing.net\">Boing Boing</a>.</p>",
